From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Subject: [PATCH] cts: latency balancing times only the clock network
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The latency balancer reads the clock arrival at each sink and nothing
else, but LatencyBalancer::initSta called updateTiming(false), which
finds every arrival in the design. Ask for the clock arrivals. With 0206,
XSTile's Top CTS on OpenROAD master peaks at 47.8 GB of heap instead of
101.8 GB and runs in 609 s instead of 1,045 s; the checkpoint after CTS
is byte-identical. Without 0206 it times the same arrivals as before.

Upstream as The-OpenROAD-Project/OpenROAD#12147; retires with the
//:bump onto an OpenROAD that has it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Øyvind Harboe <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
---
diff --git a/src/cts/src/LatencyBalancer.cpp b/src/cts/src/LatencyBalancer.cpp
index 37d1c00f8d..5e666971a2 100644
--- a/src/cts/src/LatencyBalancer.cpp
+++ b/src/cts/src/LatencyBalancer.cpp
@@ -87,7 +87,8 @@ void LatencyBalancer::initSta()
   for (auto mode : openSta_->modes()) {
     openSta_->ensureClkNetwork(mode);
   }
-  openSta_->updateTiming(false);
+  // Only clock arrivals at the sinks are read; data arrivals are not.
+  openSta_->ensureClkArrivals();
   timingGraph_ = openSta_->graph();
 }
 
